    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation says the low-resolution image becomes a dense feature field, then windowing partitions that field without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field. The feature field is the persistent carrier the compact thought process reads and updates. Windowing partitions that field into tokens for processing. The windowed tokens keep the dense carrier present instead of replacing it with only a compact thought vector.",
